# Flask Hello World

This sample project demonstrates a simple Flask application with tests and an Nginx reverse proxy in front.

## Run the application

Build and start the stack using Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Once running, open [http://localhost:8080/](http://localhost:8080/) to see the "Hello, World!" message.

The [http://localhost:8080/test](http://localhost:8080/test) endpoint displays the command for running the test suite. It does not execute tests for each HTTP request.

## Run the tests

With Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose exec app pytest -q
```

Or locally:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
pytest -q
```

The Docker image installs the dependencies in `requirements.txt`, including pytest.
